{{Documentation|self_doc=true}}
This template is for displaying a difficulty level out of 12 stars in-line.

==Parameters==
''The difficulty works in the exact same way as [[Template:Map Stars]].''

<pre>{{Stars|difficulty}}</pre>
<code>difficulty</code> is a numerical representation of the map difficulty. It is determined by interpreting the stars in a difficulty as a binary number with the most significant bit on the right (reversed in simple terms) with an empty star being 0 and a filled star being 1. For example, if the 3rd and 8th stars are filled, the number is 2^2 + 2^7 = 132.

==Usage==
<pre>{{Stars|384}}</pre>
===Result===
{{Stars|384}}